          "date": "2026-11-09 15:42:48.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21164 libcfs: open dump files with init's fs in kthreads",
        "message": "LU-21164 libcfs: open dump files with init's fs in kthreads\n\nLinux 7.3 starts all kthreads in an empty nullfs root, so path\nlookups from kthread context fail with -ENOENT unless they switch to\ninit's filesystem state with scoped_with_init_fs(). Lustre opens\nfiles by absolute path from kthreads to dump the debug log\n(debug_path, the debug daemon) and pages with checksum errors, so on\n7.3 these all fail and nothing is written, e.g.:\n\n  can't open /tmp/f60f.sanity.1793998958.261983 for dump: rc = -2\n\nThis breaks sanity test_60f, test_77c, test_170 and test_410.\n\nWrap these lookups in scoped_with_init_fs(): the debug log dump in\nlibcfs_debug_dumplog_internal(), the debug daemon file in\ntracefiled(), the checksum dumps on the client and the server, and\nthe kinode test thread. Dumps requested by \"lctl dk\" still resolve\nthe path in the caller's context. Add a configure check for\nscoped_with_init_fs(), and make it a no-op on older kernels, where\nkthreads use init's root.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I1d51e67a7b4250cc77b2b550c2a0c9cba2b74c14\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
